# The scenes of the property-based-testing deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# property-based-testing.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in property-based-testing.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add jetCheck to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/jetcheck/" "gradle/libs.versions.toml"

## Scene 2: step 2, the test dependency
note "Step 2: add it as a test dependency. A switch chooses which splitter the tests run against."
show lessons/property-based-testing/example/build.gradle.kts "/libs.jetcheck/" "lesson build file: dependencies" --zoom 9
show lessons/property-based-testing/example/build.gradle.kts "/^tasks.test/" "lesson build file: tests"

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: everyone pays the same, and the first person pays whatever is left over."
show FirstPayerSplitter 14 19 --zoom 17

## Scene 4: the example tests
note "*Example* tests: each checks one case its author thought of."
show SplitterExampleTest 12 26

## Scene 5: the property test
note "The *property* test: three rules for every bill, checked on a hundred random bills."
show SplitterPropertyTest 30 47 --zoom 33-34 --mark 44-46

## Scene 6: the property finds a bug
note "Run the tests against the splitter in use today:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:property-based-testing:test -Pcode=today"
callout "3 cents between 4 people: the first person pays all 3. None of the example tests checked a bill like this."

## Scene 7: the fair splitter
note "The fair splitter shares the leftover cents one each:"
show FairSplitter 9 16 --zoom 13
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:property-based-testing:test"
callout "Every property holds, for every bill jetCheck tried."
